# CODEOWNERS — jolarca-vendor
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TREATING THIS FILE AS A CONTROL.
#
# This file provides ROUTING AND ATTRIBUTION. It is NOT an approval control for
# this repository, for two independent reasons:
#
#   1. `require_code_owner_reviews` is FALSE for jolarca-vendor in
#      jolarca-control/repos/jolarca-vendor.yml. Nothing blocks a merge on the
#      strength of this file.
#   2. `required_approving_review_count` is 0 and there is exactly one operator.
#      The only resolvable owner is the person authoring the change, so a
#      code-owner review would be self-review, which provides no independence.
#
# The organisation has no teams. Pointing this file at a team that does not exist
# makes it silently unresolvable — a control that is present in configuration and
# never fires, which is worse than no control because it appears on a checklist.
# It therefore names a real user account, which is resolvable and honest about
# what it can do.
#
# The compensating controls for the absence of independent review are the
# automated gates in .github/workflows/ci.yml and the annual external audit.
# See docs/solo-operator-controls.md for what they do and do not prove.
#
# When a second operator is onboarded, this file should be updated to name both
# and `require_code_owner_reviews` raised via jolarca-control. That is the trigger
# recorded in the estate deviation register for closing the solo-era deviations.

# Everything, by default.
